<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:45Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Police make seventh arrest over UK airbase incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60bdd7d611497712b5a923a930d8e8301399f95d0d41ebd4be5e03a3ab2b6f8c</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:51:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident--a2cfc3b816d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident" /><summary type="html">A seventh man was arrested Tuesday over a major incident last month at a British military airbase used by the United States to launch strikes on Iran, police said. The arrest came a day after President Donald Trump said the United States had withdrawn all B-1 bombers from RAF Fairford because of "threats" he believed were linked to Tehran. A 22-year-old British male was arrested in London "on suspicion of preparation of terrorist acts", Britain's Counter-Terrorism Policing network said in a statement. Six men in their 20s have already been arrested and released on bail after three suspicious vans were stopped near the base in southwest England on September 27. FRANCE 24's Bénédicte Paviot reports from London.</summary></entry><entry><title>Calls to block social media platforms for minors in France amid school protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b7c79d6ef95574dcfb4fd9f4d42a488609766d6aa3bafeaa9353a06de07ff84</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:47:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/calls-to-block-social-media-platforms-for-minors-in-france-amid-school-protests--b44929c55975.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/calls-to-block-social-media-platforms-for-minors-in-france-amid-school-protests" /><summary type="html">One factor accelerating these student protest is social media, and its being boosted even more by artificial intelligence. Some French mayors have even called for social media platforms to be temporarily blocked for minors. Our colleauges at France 2 took a look at the impact</summary></entry><entry><title>German ex-spy chief arrested for suspected espionage, treason</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5babfdabdd4950f976dc6d0ee1643083a96a23972837b014ed0796f994656d2</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:42:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason--cbca89fe2a12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason" /><summary type="html">A former German spy chief was arrested Tuesday on suspicion of espionage and treason, an embarrassing case at a time when the country is seeking to broaden the powers of its intelligence agencies. August Hanning, who ran Germany's BND foreign intelligence agency from 1998 to 2005, is accused of espionage, treason and working for foreign intelligence services, federal prosecutors said. FRANCE 24's Nick Holdsworth reports from Berlin.</summary></entry><entry><title>'We're fed up': Paris students rise up in a movement that shows no sign of slowing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b61093ba94a92a83c70f971bd55fcd94527864da3f9c765ae0828d7d612a187</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:41:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261006-we-re-fed-up-paris-students-rise-up-in-a-movement-that-shows-no-sign-of-slowing--af976d777fba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261006-we-re-fed-up-paris-students-rise-up-in-a-movement-that-shows-no-sign-of-slowing" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of students and their supporters took part in nationwide protests across France on Tuesday after weeks of student barricades protesting school conditions.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Students, unions and teachers in mass movement to demand better learning conditions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53dd6ece4cde1761fc2313d1cc7f265748156321c7d4b1cbb705dfbdef10c93e</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:39:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/students-unions-and-teachers-in-mass-movement-to-demand-better-learning-conditions--8c9b78ca5575.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/students-unions-and-teachers-in-mass-movement-to-demand-better-learning-conditions" /><summary type="html">A quarter of a million demonstrators took to the streets across France on Tuesday as unions and teachers joined high school students demanding better learning conditions in protests that later descended into sporadic clashes with security forces. A French policeman was on Tuesday charged with violence over the firing of a tear gas grenade last week at close range at a 14-year-old student during the high school protests that have shaken the country, the prosecutor said. Reporting from central Paris, FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin says the protesters are adamant that "this is not it, this movement will continue, we want concrete actions from the government".</summary></entry><entry><title>France erupts overs schools: Why the violence surrounding surprise movement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acadfed9e9e64bed113aa712ab986b022fbfaa8ed92b1d8426e3762626b68199</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:12:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261006-france-erupts-overs-schools-why-the-violence-surrounding-surprise-movement--c22593653ff3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261006-france-erupts-overs-schools-why-the-violence-surrounding-surprise-movement" /><summary type="html">It’s a protest movement that a broke, lame-duck French government did not see coming. Civil servants this Tuesday joining high schoolers now in their third week of picketing over long-deteriorating classroom conditions. The usual recipe for wearing down movements in France has recently been to match eventual violence with a heavy hand, the escalation turning the silent majority against the protesters as was the case with the pre-Covid Yellow Vests movement.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>'Colossal failure: Death penalty system in America is a broken process from start to finish'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1e3f5e6ee7cd194b4f169d04bc85bb4f29d3779687c7fa0997ea81c1aa327a7</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/colossal-failure-death-penalty-system-in-america-is-a-broken-process-from-start-to-finish--4aeddd5f6ac1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/colossal-failure-death-penalty-system-in-america-is-a-broken-process-from-start-to-finish" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Reed Brody, international human rights lawyer and former New York assistant attorney general. According to Brody, the botched execution of Christa Pike reflects a much larger problem: the relationship between capital punishment, institutional failure, due process, and human dignity. The technical failure of lethal injection exposes weaknesses throughout the legal architecture surrounding the death penalty, from the quality and adequacy of defense representation to the profound disparities between jurisdictions and the difficulties states face in administering executions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil 'has moved to the right progressively over the last two decades', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cecb29b93c7d6a9c8e813213a9825eeac58c280b395ed114711f1d7d750b694b</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:05:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261006-brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says--0d01da482669.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261006-brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Senator Flavio Bolsonaro received on Monday endorsements ​from Ronaldo Caiado and Romeu Zema, two right-wing politicians who ran against him in Sunday's first-round vote, ​for ‌the runoff against President Luiz ⁠Inacio Lula da Silva later this month. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Anthony Pereira, Executive Director of the Stone Center for Latin American Studies at Tulane University, says that "Lula's path to victory lies in mobilising voters who didn't vote in the first round" while Flavio Bolsonaro "will probably benefit from the voters who voted for other right-wing candidates and who will simply migrate to him, so it looks a lot easier for Flavio to win the second round than it does for Lula".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil 'has moved to the right progressively over the last two decades', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71481e8bd3445f94e9444c6bb53e246d688a61b149ea199dd0980243aecf1885</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:03:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says--155757afd4f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Senator Flavio Bolsonaro received on Monday endorsements ​from Ronaldo Caiado and Romeu Zema, two right-wing politicians who ran against him in Sunday's first-round vote, ​for ‌the runoff against President Luiz ⁠Inacio Lula da Silva later this month. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Anthony Pereira, Executive Director of the Stone Center for Latin American Studies at Tulane University, says that "Lula's path to victory lies in mobilising voters who didn't vote in the first round" while Flavio Bolsonaro "will probably benefit from the voters who voted for other right-wing candidates and who will simply migrate to him, so it looks a lot easier for Flavio to win the second round than it does for Lula".</summary></entry><entry><title>Paramount completes takeover of Warner Bros, creating media behemoth Skydance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1a9cd0a04e241c9acd6e6c253db6c86c30788522c6fabf04209e5879c3192cc</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:23:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-paramount-completes-takeover-of-warner-bros-creating-media-behemoth-skydance--ef54048f63ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-paramount-completes-takeover-of-warner-bros-creating-media-behemoth-skydance" /><summary type="html">Paramount completed its acquisition of Warner Bros Discover on Tuesday, after a bidding war against Netflix. The deal closed following federal approval of a settlement between Paramount and 12 US states that tried to block the transaction on antitrust grounds. Opponents in the movie industry warned of job cuts, while media groups said Warner-owned CNN's independence could be compromised.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands demand better education in demonstrations across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96a66b2d9a18ff66f14ef5d55c50fb819d39966f5928e527328e14370cc05f06</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:04:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-tens-of-thousands-demand-better-education-in-demonstrations-across-france--d6a25e972eb7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-tens-of-thousands-demand-better-education-in-demonstrations-across-france" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of demonstrators took to the streets across France on Tuesday, as unions and teachers joined high school students who for days have been demanding better learning conditions in protests punctuated by violent confrontations.</summary></entry><entry><title>Norway eyes temporary ban of smart glasses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dfbaf37d22b3a8128e43c03414fc17ce14d4a8f87be25f4ec4750dadfe371986</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:03:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-norway-eyes-temporary-ban-of-smart-glasses--d50ed79d436e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-norway-eyes-temporary-ban-of-smart-glasses" /><summary type="html">Norway's government said Monday it wants a temporary ban on the use of smart glasses in certain public places, citing privacy concerns, notably recording images without the knowledge of those filmed. The ban could apply to parks, beaches, museums, shopping centres, schools, daycare centres, healthcare facilities, gyms and public events.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Tense' atmosphere as tens of thousands join French student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96bda37bcc003fb7298214c029b67e7d190683eeaf3d67f02fa43dcfb8d94148</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:02:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-tense-atmosphere-as-tens-of-thousands-join-french-student-protests--6c713aa473d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-tense-atmosphere-as-tens-of-thousands-join-french-student-protests" /><summary type="html">Police fired tear gas at ​protesters blockading French high schools on Tuesday as students, teachers and parents took to the streets on the biggest day of action in a wave of demonstrations against understaffed and dilapidated classrooms. Reporting from a march in Paris, France 24's Claire Paccalin says that the demonstration there has been peaceful so far, though the atmosphere is "tense" with a "heavy police presence".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine fires nearly 900 drones at Russia, says Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee88aff2f223f217999fe52f83320c2f5e2050b77eff270374f7162bf29b88b7</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:01:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ukraine-fires-nearly-900-drones-at-russia-says-moscow--4deb9ecc93df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ukraine-fires-nearly-900-drones-at-russia-says-moscow" /><summary type="html">Russian air defenses intercepted nearly 900 Ukrainian drones overnight over multiple regions of the country, as well as the occupied Crimean Peninsula and the Sea of Azov, the Defense Ministry in Moscow said Tuesday. If the figures accurate, it would make it one of the largest Ukrainian drone strikes on Russia since the start of the war, says France 24's correspondent Gulliver Cragg.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paris Fashion Week: Nicole Kidman, Dua Lipa and Rihanna light up the front row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51763cd5d4892e39b27d850bf20a23fdb22a96e4cade0b4d157a81bb87ce82df</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:56:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261006-paris-fashion-week-nicole-kidman-dua-lipa-and-rihanna-light-up-the-front-row--5a36fd23f918.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261006-paris-fashion-week-nicole-kidman-dua-lipa-and-rihanna-light-up-the-front-row" /><summary type="html">Paris is once again the centre of planet fashion, as the spring-summer 2027 collections take over the catwalks. Simon Moritz takes us through the big hitters, starting with Matthieu Blazy’s exploration of the different women who made up Gabrielle Chanel, as he goes from strength to strength at the prestigious fashion house. We also discuss the comings and goings at YSL, Balenciaga and Dior, and meet Lithuanian designer Juozas Statkevicius as he puts his national heritage in the spotlight.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports first-ever Ebola death after patient returns from DR Congo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e4249ed69944e7b7a2a35a54d7192142af9434ab6600531ff91f65497f9e412</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:41:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261006-kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death-after-patient-returns-from-dr-congo--ad7202bd54ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261006-kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death-after-patient-returns-from-dr-congo" /><summary type="html">Kenya on Tuesday reported its first-ever Ebola death after a Kenyan national who had been living in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DR Congo) died after returning to the country. Kenya is the fourth country to record an Ebola case in the current outbreak, which was declared in eastern DR Congo in mid-May.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'We were naive' about Hamas, Israeli ex-hostage Shoshan Haran says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f447caaaf97a5dea87e9d7177d13c9aaccf8887de6e4e99146ac538d2ccc281</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:03:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says--83490e71ebdf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israeli former hostage Shoshan Haran said "we were naive" about Hamas before the October 7, 2023 attack on her kibbutz. Held in Gaza for 50 days, she recalled refusing to "show weakness" to her captors. She also called the accusations of genocide against Israel "a lie" and shared her late husband's last words.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>French students looking for protests 'to become a major movement'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91a204b6531cb28520ec7013fb13b5a992bbb307d6a53f35543f43a3ec04b3d6</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:03:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:49:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-french-students-looking-for-protests-to-become-a-major-movement--4e68dd5acbe8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-french-students-looking-for-protests-to-become-a-major-movement" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of demonstrators marched in cities across France on Tuesday in support of protests by school pupils demanding more education funding, increasing pressure on the government of outgoing President Emmanuel Macron. With teachers and trade unions joining the march, the students are seeking to turn the protests into a "major social movement" to increase pressure on the government, says France 24's Marc Perelman.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: French PM denies 'police repression', suspends classes as clashes erupt at student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ecaa2290f77f0b0ab8060f17cf1fc2eff375315dc0f576bca57417400fce5d4</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:03:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:21:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students--df93e10e4e3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students" /></entry><entry><title>'Busification': Inside Ukraine’s controversial recruitment practices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e59e8a9b09288bf523c221ef2d5f3f6843a2c75f9deb6dfbf117f775dcae16e9</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:03:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:19:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-busification-inside-ukraine-s-controversial-recruitment-practices--28bf4e6cdcb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-busification-inside-ukraine-s-controversial-recruitment-practices" /><summary type="html">Recent reports and videos of alleged recruitment irregularities are fuelling tensions between mobilisation authorities and Ukrainian society, while raising questions about the oversight and implementation of military recruitment.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French students: What do they want?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6354d460f687086655c57c004494e9ade8e8ac2221d90423d53cc59c3e1d9916</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:03:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:16:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261006-french-students-what-do-they-want--39b1aa2a286e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261006-french-students-what-do-they-want" /><summary type="html">We take a look at what exactly French high school students are demanding in their nationwide blockades. From crumbling buildings, to absent teachers who are not replaced, to applying to university, we take a look at what has created so much anger among French teens. We also draw parallels between this movement and that of the Yellow Vests.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia 'fears Tigray conflict could get out of control'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfdbbfeb6e95aa699c3125fd39c31eea4ca33ebdca94a8b36e56943f64147a5d</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:03:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ethiopia-fears-tigray-conflict-could-get-out-of-control--71887e6b2a41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ethiopia-fears-tigray-conflict-could-get-out-of-control" /><summary type="html">Airstrikes and artillery fire rocked northern Ethiopia's Tigray region overnight into Monday, aid sources said, in clashes between federal government and rebel forces that have raised fears of wider fighting. France 24's Philip Turle says that the Ethiopian government is pushing into Tigray territory amid fears the conflict "could get out of control".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian drones kill two, hit fuel hub in one of biggest attacks on Moscow region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f49cfdfb93c5de76edc8264ba8d04406087bd09a7bca25592e7e644da15a9e1e</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:03:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:07:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ukrainian-drones-kill-two-hit-fuel-hub-in-one-of-biggest-attacks-on-moscow-region--ad9c4c4026d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ukrainian-drones-kill-two-hit-fuel-hub-in-one-of-biggest-attacks-on-moscow-region" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian ​drones killed two people and hit a major fuel depot overnight in one of the biggest attacks of ​the war on Moscow and the surrounding region. France 24's Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>India opposition parties rally for election chief’s exit over voter list changes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d58a3d7d910fcf40d85beb5b4e3bf0de12e5f66a736bdf0c2f7a2aa55a6581b</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:03:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:06:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-india-opposition-parties-rally-for-election-chief-s-exit-over-voter-list-changes--652cb77cb918.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-india-opposition-parties-rally-for-election-chief-s-exit-over-voter-list-changes" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties held protests in India’s capital New Delhi on Tuesday, demanding the resignation of the country’s election chief over a contentious revision of voter lists as hundreds of police personnel were deployed across the heart of the city. Tuesday’s demonstration is the latest in a series of near-daily protests beginning last week by student groups, opposition parties and India's “Cockroach” youth movement.</summary></entry></feed>
